UID:melissa-travel-e470a00c379e@jstravelschedule.netlify.app
DTSTAMP:20260629T204502Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260702
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260708
SUMMARY:Jason: Philadelphia\, PA
DESCRIPTION:NEP Bishops & Media - Philadelphia\n\nStatus: Booked\nHotel: So
 nesta Philadelphia Rittenhouse Square\, event/block NEP Bishops & Media - P
 hiladelphia. Confirmation QQAX2KIP for Jason Shanks.\nStay: arrive Thu Jul
  2\, depart Mon Jul 6. Room type: Deluxe - Two Queens\; 1 room\, 2 guests.
  Rate shown in confirmation: $229/night\; grand total $1\,065.86.\nCancella
 tion: cancel by 4:00 PM local hotel time the day before arrival to avoid on
 e night room/tax penalty.\nNEC staff lodging listed for Jason Shanks\, Ephr
 em Shanks\, Sarah Houde\, Maria Benes\, and Haley Rossi at Sonesta Rittenho
 use Square\, 1800 Market Street\, less than a mile from the Cathedral Basil
 ica.\nThu Jul 2: Pilgrim team expected to arrive 3:00-4:00 PM\; Father Gill
  should receive ETA once team is on the road. Jason and Ephrem's PHL arriva
 l time / AA flight number still TBD.\nThu Jul 2: Sarah arrives PHL 4:14 PM
  on DL 5706\; Maria arrives PHL 6:00 PM\, Southwest flight number TBD. Sara
 h will Uber to hotel and meet team at Cathedral Basilica for dinner.\nThu J
 ul 2: 5:30 PM dinner at Cathedral Basilica\, then 7:00 PM Young Adult Holy
  Hour. Overnight adoration follows with local adorers filling spots.\nFri J
 ul 3: Christ in the City service day. 8:30 AM training at Cathedral Basilic
 a Neumann Room\; 9:15 AM-noon walk through city center to visit with homele
 ss\; concludes with 12:05 PM Sung Mass and boxed lunches.\nFri Jul 3 civic
  options: 11:00 AM Pope Leo Liberty Medal video address at Independence Mal
 l\; noon-4:00 PM Salute to Independence parade\; 5:00 PM food trucks/block
  party and 7:00-9:00 PM Philly Pops Concert at Independence National Histor
 ical Park.\nSat Jul 4: Mary Carmen's birthday. Cabrini film showings at Cat
 hedral Basilica at 10:00 AM\, 1:00 PM\, and 3:30 PM\, though pilgrims alrea
 dy saw the film in Charlotte.\nSat Jul 4: Cathedral day includes 12:05 PM S
 ung Mass\, street-fair lunch\, 4:30 PM Family Rosary Across America\, 5:15
  PM Vigil Mass\, dinner after Mass\, and 7:00 PM NEC Staff & Pilgrim Dinner
  with Relevant Radio. Location still TBD.\nSat Jul 4 follow-up: confirm whe
 n RR is arriving / setting up equipment\; Jason asked if Father Rocky can a
 ttend dinner\; invite Archbishop Perez and Bishop Pohlmeier once time/locat
 ion are known.\nSat Jul 4 civic options: Historic Germantown all day\; FIFA
  Fan Festival noon-4:00 PM at Lemon Hill\; World Cup game 5:00 PM at Lincol
 n Financial Field\; Benjamin Franklin Parkway concert/fireworks 5:00 PM-mid
 night\, fireworks at 11:45 PM.\nSun Jul 5: Cathedral revised Mass schedule
  is 7:30 AM\, 9:00 AM\, 11:00 AM\, 1:00 PM Spanish/Chapel. Confessions at 8
 :30 AM and 12:30 PM Spanish/Chapel.\nSun Jul 5: team arrival time and reser
 ved parking locations still TBD for NEP van\, Rachel's car\, and Sarah's pa
 rents' car.\nSun Jul 5: 10:50 AM? Pope Leo video address before 11:00 AM So
 lemn Mass\; exact time awaiting EWTN confirmation. Perpetual Pilgrims bring
  prayer intentions to altar during offertory.\nSun Jul 5: Heavy snacks in D
 rexel Hall after Mass for pilgrims/staff to pack before procession\; no tim
 e for lunch before procession.\nSun Jul 5: 12:30 PM Eucharistic Procession
  from Cathedral Basilica to National Shrine of St. John Neumann at St. Pete
 r the Apostle Church\; route approx. 2 miles\, concluding with Benediction.
  NEC banner carried by archdiocesan seminarians Joshua Brooks and Ryan Scav
 nicky.\nSun Jul 5: 1:30-4:30 PM concluding fellowship reception at St. Pete
 r the Apostle / Shrine of St. John Neumann\, with 2:00 PM press conference
  during reception. Reception has light appetizers only\, likely not enough
  for dinner.\nSun Jul 5 follow-up: decide whether NEC should arrange team d
 inner\; Maria Benes offered to look into a reservation.\nMon Jul 6: Perpetu
 al Pilgrim team departs for post-NEP retreat at IHM Spirituality Center\, 2
 10 IHM Drive\, Malvern\, PA 19355\; departure time TBD.\nMon Jul 6: 6:45 PM
  meet Tim Flanagan in the lobby at Four Seasons Hotel Philadelphia\, One N
  19th Street. Tim is flying up from Orlando with ETA 5:15 PM and will advis
 e if delayed. Dinner with Drew Peloubet\, Board Chair\, and Bill Orosz\, fo
 rmer Board Chair\; Martha Ortiz\, Vice Chair\, may join.\nTue Jul 7: 9:15 A
 M meet Tim Flanagan in the Four Seasons lobby. Conference room available un
 til 2:00 PM\; Jason can leave whenever best for his flight. Tim will send a
  separate text with Dan's information.\nCLI dinner prep: Drew Peloubet is C
 LI Board Chair\, a Tampa-based Catholic philanthropist/business leader\, fo
 rmer CEO/majority shareholder of Restaurant Magic\, and a major CLI support
 er with ties to Christ the King parish\, Legatus\, FOCUS\, the Diocese of S
 t. Petersburg\, Feeding Tampa Bay\, Food For The Poor\, and Haiti projects.
 \nCLI dinner prep: Bill Orosz is Chair Emeritus / former CLI Board Chair\,
  an Orlando real estate developer and philanthropist associated with the Or
 osz family/Hanover Capital legacy\; CLI notes he has built more than 26\,00
 0 homes and developed more than 85 residential communities. He is founding
  chair of the Catholic Foundation of Central Florida and has chaired the Di
 ocese of Orlando Finance Committee.\nCLI dinner prep: Martha Ortiz is CLI V
 ice Chair\, a Philadelphia-based retired investment professional and former
  principal of Aronson\, Johnson\, Ortiz. Her background includes portfolio
  management/trading\, Harvard and Wharton degrees\, CFA and Chartered Inves
 tment Counselor credentials\, and service with The Baldwin School\, The Hav
 erford School\, St. Margaret's Church in Narberth\, and the Cathedral Basil
 ica of Saints Peter and Paul.\nSpans the July 4th holiday.\n\nView live: ht
 tps://jstravelschedule.netlify.app
LOCATION:Philadelphia\, PA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
